tic equation (i.e. the closedloop<br />\npoles) of the closed-loop system 1 + KG(s) = 0 as the gain &ldquo;K&rdquo; varies from 0 to &infin;. The root<br />\nlocus is symmetric about the real axis and not the imaginary axis. Hence, only statements (a) and<br />\n(b) are correct.</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":12,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>The block diagram of a system is shown in the figure,</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/41a204c2b1fb01b6681bf60a6051129ff3a9eae3.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>Then whole system is equivalent to</div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> An integrator with gain = 0.5</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> A differentiator with gain = 2</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> First order system</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> Zero order system</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/f08ccbd23bec23d7d6d5521c8f762c52447a3233.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":13,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A phase lag compensator is to be added to provide maximum phase lag of 45° at 3 rad/sec. The pole of lag compensator in s-plane is located at _______ rad/sec. (upto one decimal place)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"-7.2","high":"-7.2"},"solution":"<p>-7.2 (-8.1 - -6.2)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/9b54322548a329f5b459b0895a8e0c3a5fb285f0.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":14,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Transfer function of a first order system is given by</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/6a4b5773ad6ef87dfb7160ce4be3626cb58b79b7.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>\n<div>Impulse response of the system is,</div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/67d87c7e41ffb0d719c6c37e98408d4981f576e4.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/7787d9c0f510f41c3382484ecd116ed18764ca3e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/a10cfddf8e094f495d48d5e0411cbd4d1ade3c01.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/183b54b14f6558f86d45c61f6c8c30e310fb685b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/efefd874151605ba136ca5b3553cb5bbfd624696.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":15,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Consider the system with following open loop transfer function:</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/33146ce0990edfa88ad542fdd3a8962281e3fe04.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>\n<div>In a root locus plot, the value of <em>K</em> at point <img src=\"/media/3c79f1358016085ebab557d153429406467ad1b6.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> is _______ .</div></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"12","high":"12"},"solution":"<p>12.0 (10.5 - 13.0)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/a1064a84f1004e5abab5addaf1efb4a7a8a27f08.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":16,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>Loop transfer function of a feedback system is <em>G</em>(<em>s</em>)<em>H</em>(<em>s</em>) = <img src=\"/media/b7329a93bb94cf76566e767991a97e931a1bbe2f.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> Then, the Nyquist plot of <em>G</em>(<em>s</em>)<em>H</em>(<em>s</em>) encircles –1 + <em>j</em>0</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> once in clockwise direction</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> does not encircle</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> once in anticlockwise dir